---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="Project information — Caelora" noindex>
  <main id="main" class="container document">
    <span class="eyebrow">Project information</span>
    <h1>A world in development.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Caelora is an independent native Windows game in development. This website presents the
      project's direction, concept art and 3D model studies, and the development journal.
    </p>
    <h2>Status as of 12 November 2026</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No public build, release date or price has been announced.</li>
      <li>Purchases, game ownership and launcher downloads are not available.</li>
      <li>
        Account services are not open yet: registration and sign-in cannot be completed until the
        platform service is deployed.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="community">Community & support</h2>
    <p>
      Official community channels and a support contact have not been published yet. They will be
      announced in the <a href="/journal/">development journal</a> when they exist. Until then you
      can follow development with the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 id="legal">Legal & privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The public website does not offer payments, analytics, advertising, newsletters or sign-up
      forms, and sets no cookies. When account services open, they will use essential authentication
      and CSRF cookies and store an email address, display name, password hash, browser sessions and
      security events.
    </p>
    <p>
      Publisher details, contact information, terms of sale, refund policy and a deployment-specific
      privacy notice will be published before account registration or commerce becomes available.
    </p>
    <p>
      Images are concept art and 3D model studies, not gameplay footage, and may change during
      development. Third-party font licences are distributed with the project source.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/">
      <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to Caelora
    </a>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
